ARCHITECTURE NOTE: 5-file A7 page set mirroring the sibling DrivesListPage / RegenEfficiencyPage / TripPlannerPage
precedent. The view (composable) performs NO HTTP — it collects StateFlow<UiState<…>> from the ViewModel, which
binds the shared-core repositories/use-cases (ADR-004) through the narrow MapOverviewPageSource seam:
  • useVehicles            → HttpVehiclesRepository.vehicles()            GET /vehicles            (declared source)
  • useVehiclePositions    → HttpVehiclesRepository.vehiclePositions(id,50) GET /vehicles/{id}/positions?limit=50
  • useLocationSnapshotLatest → HttpVehiclesRepository.locationSnapshotLatest(id) GET /location-snapshots/latest
  • useUnits/useFormatting → SettingsStore.settings()                     GET /settings
  • useSelectedVehicle     → SelectedVehicleStore (effective id self-heals to the first vehicle — web default).
The host (MapOverviewPageHost) constructs the shared HttpVehiclesRepository over the SAME resilient client + offline
cache the DataContainer's VehiclesStore uses (so ADR-013 freshness + SI-verbatim caching are identical), giving the
page a deterministic retry that re-fetches via the refresh trigger (DrivesList precedent). The page-VM projects each
feed onto the shared lifecycle-aware UiState via BaseFeedViewModel.asUiState (the standard A7 page-VM job).

NAV NOTE: the `liveMap` /live destination already exists in Destinations.kt (page("liveMap","/live",NavGroup.Maps));
this prompt only wires the host (MapOverviewPageHost.register() in TeslaSyncApplication) — no fabricated destination.
The "Quick Links" buttons navigate to the registered navigationRoute/geofences/locations destinations via their
app-scheme deep link (teslasync://app/…, declared in AndroidManifest) using LocalUriHandler — the sibling
FeedbackQueuePage precedent; no dead buttons.

SI NOTE (the prompt's Units rule + ADR-013): decode + derivation stay SI end-to-end (degrees, m/s, metres); the only
display conversion is at the render boundary via MapOverviewDisplayPrefs (shared convertSpeedFromSI /
convertDistanceFromSI + ChartFormat). Speed AND odometer are converted from SI through the user's unit prefs — the
odometer correctly uses convertDistanceFromSI(metres) rather than transplanting the web's raw `fmtNumber(odometer)`
(an un-converted web display quirk); the prompt mandates "format at the display boundary with the shared SI
converters — never store/compute non-SI", so the SI-canonical conversion is the faithful behaviour.

STRINGS NOTE: 33 of the 34 mapOverview keys + error.loadFailed already existed in res/values/strings.xml; 2 required
keys were missing (mapOverview.noHistory, mapOverview.subtitle) and were added to values/ + values-ar/ + values-he/
(English fallback, matching the catalog's existing ar/he-as-fallback convention). All 35 visible literals resolve
via stringResource(); zero hardcoded text in the page (verified: only detekt rule-name strings, destination ids, and
the internal marker id "vehicle" — none user-visible).

ICONS NOTE: material-icons-extended is intentionally not a dependency (see components/maps/MapsGlyphs.kt), so the
lucide glyphs the web page uses (Gauge/Compass/MapPin/Clock/Home/Briefcase/Link2/Fence/AlertCircle) are authored as
24×24 stroked ImageVectors in MapOverviewPageIcons.kt; the map-control glyphs already in MapsGlyphs
(Navigation/Route/Crosshair) are reused for the odometer row + quick links (DRY, ADR-006).

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' -> app/); the prompt
snippet's ':app:' is the same module (documented alias, as in every sibling P3/A* gate log).

